course: dictionary
lesson: 4837
title: Hybrid: mixed things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hybrid is something made by mixing two different things. In science, a hybrid is a plant or animal whose parents are two different kinds. A mule is a hybrid: its parents are a horse and a donkey.
explain: Hybrid can also describe something that mixes two things. «A hybrid car has both a petrol engine and an electric motor with a small battery.» The clue is the word both: the car uses two kinds of power, so hybrid means mixed.
explain: Look at the words around hybrid to check its meaning. Phrases like «a hybrid of» (a mix of two things) and «hybrid working» (some work at home, some at the office) show the same idea. Ask yourself: are two different things joined together?
fact: A hybrid is a plant or animal whose parents are two different kinds.
fact: A mule is a hybrid: its parents are a horse and a donkey.
fact: A hybrid can also be anything that mixes two different things.
fact: «Hybrid car» means a car that uses petrol and electricity together.
fact: Young hybrids like mules often cannot have babies of their own.
exercise: «A hybrid car has both a petrol engine and an electric motor.» What does hybrid mean here? | Made only of metal | Very fast and silent | Old and broken | *Mixed, using two kinds of power
exercise: A mule is a hybrid. What are its parents? | Two donkeys | *A horse and a donkey | Two horses | A cow and a sheep
exercise: Which phrase means some lessons at school and some online? | *Hybrid learning | Hybrid sofa | Hybrid lamp | Hybrid cloud
test: «Hybrid working» means what? | Working only at night | Working with animals | *Some work at home and some in the office | Not working at all
test: Which of these is a hybrid? | A bicycle | A cat | *A mule | A rock
exam: Hybrid cars use less fuel because they | run on water only | have no engine at all | never need a battery | *switch between petrol and electric power
